      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: protect uncovered cleanup window in runCodexAppServerAttempt (#99271)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`runCodexAppServerAttempt` has a ~160-line window between turn acceptance and the cleanup `finally` where any synchronous throw leaks notification/request handlers on the shared Codex pooled client, leaves the shared-client lease unreleased, and leaves a phantom active-run handle. This corrupts the session for subsequent attempts and is the structural reason `run-attempt.ts` has the highest fix churn in the repo (219 fix-type commits in 6 months).\n\n## Summary\n\n`runCodexAppServerAttempt` in `extensions/codex/src/app-server/run-attempt.ts` had an uncovered exception window: the single cleanup `finally` started ~160 lines too late, leaving every post-turn-accept resource (notification/request handlers, event projector, steering queue, close handler, abort listener, active-run handle, shared-client lease) unprotected against synchronous throws.\n\n### Change\n\nMove the cleanup try boundary from just before `await completion` to right after turn acceptance (line 2938, +0 behavior change), so the single existing `finally` covers **all** resources acquired in the ~160-line setup window.\n\n- Before: only `attachBackend` + `setActiveEmbeddedRun` were try-protected (partial fix)\n- After: user-input bridge, projector, steering queue, handlers, close handler, abort listener, reply backend, active-run handle → all covered by one `finally`\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] **Inject test** (`run-attempt.cleanup-inject.test.ts`): patches `replyOperation.attachBackend` to throw synchronously, asserts `detachBackend` fires (proves full cleanup path)\n- [x] `run-attempt.dynamic-tools.test.ts` (8 tests) — passed\n- [x] `run-attempt.hooks.test.ts` (21 tests) — passed  \n- [x] `run-attempt.native-hook-relay.test.ts` (18 tests) — passed\n- [x] `attempt-client-cleanup.test.ts` (2 tests) — passed\n\n## Evidence\n\n**L2 — local vitest inject test** + full regression suite:\n\n```bash\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/codex/src/app-server/run-attempt.cleanup-inject.test.ts\n RUN  v4.1.8 E:/Projects/skills/work/openclaw\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  1 passed (1)\n\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/codex/src/app-server/run-attempt.dynamic-tools.test.ts \\\n  extensions/codex/src/app-server/run-attempt.hooks.test.ts \\\n  extensions/codex/src/app-server/run-attempt.native-hook-relay.test.ts \\\n  extensions/codex/src/app-server/attempt-client-cleanup.test.ts\n RUN  v4.1.8 E:/Projects/skills/work/openclaw\n Test Files  4 passed (4)\n      Tests  49 passed (49)\n```\n\nBefore: `attachBackend` throwing left handlers, lease, active-run handle leaked. After: the expanded try boundary means the `finally` runs `notificationCleanup()`, `requestCleanup()`, `closeCleanup?.()`, `releaseSharedClientLeaseAndRetireOneShotClient()`, `detachBackend`, `clearActiveEmbeddedRun` — every cleanup step fires.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe `try` that owns the cleanup `finally` opened at line ~3107 (`await completion`), but all resource acquisition happened between lines ~2938–3096 — a ~160-line uncovered window.\n\n## Expected vs actual behavior\n\n| Scenario | Before | After |\n|----------|--------|-------|\n| Any synchronous throw in setup window | Handlers/lease/active-run leaked | ✅ Full cleanup fires via finally |\n| Normal completion | Unchanged | Unchanged |\n\n## Impact\n\nPrevents notification/request handler leaks on the shared Codex pooled client, shared-client lease leaks, and phantom active-run handles when setup fails. No behavior change for the normal (success) path.\n\n## Proof limitations\n\nNo live Codex attempt was executed. Evidence is a vitest inject test on the real function with a mock client — L2 (source-repro + inject test), not L3 (live failing attempt).\n\n## Linked issues\n\n- Fixes #99271",
